**/service-account*.json
**/google-services.json
# ...except the Android app's own, which has to be committed.
#
# EAS builds from the git state, so a file ignored here never reaches the build
# server and the APK ships without Firebase — which on Android means
# expo-notifications has no FCM config and the app closes straight after the
# splash screen. That is the bug this file exists to fix, and leaving it ignored
# reproduces it exactly.
#
# Unlike its neighbours above it is not a credential: it carries project
# identifiers and an API key scoped to the package name, which Google documents
# as safe to commit. The FCM service-account key, which *is* a credential, stays
# ignored by the **/service-account*.json rule and lives only in EAS.
!mobile/google-services.json
**/GoogleService-Info.plist
!**/*.example.json
**/.npmrc
!**/.npmrc.example
**/.sentryclirc
**/.netrc
**/.dev.vars
**/.dev.vars.*
!**/.dev.vars.example
id_rsa*
id_ed25519*

